 is up only 12%.\n- Pellham Power is the weak point. Caldria Ratings put it on negative watch after its equity raise failed. More debt without equity would weaken its credit metrics.\n- Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp, from 135bp in Q2 and 130bp in Q1. Borrowing is costlier but still possible.\n\n**Equity**\n- The window is effectively shut. Two utility share offerings were cut back in Q3. Pellham pulled its C$2.4B offering on 14 October because investor demand fell short.\n- Pellham plans 2027 capex up 18%. It now says it will cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and resize its roughly C$900M Q1 tender. It will also defer two substation programmes \"until financing improves\".\n\n**What this means:** Expect Pellham to scale back or defer its plan. Norvane should be able to borrow what it needs. Equity should not be counted on for either company.\n\n**Gaps:** The sources give only percentage capex growth. They have no dollar totals, funding gaps, leverage ratios, all-in yields, valuations or dilution estimates. Confidence in the direction is moderate. Confidence in the sizing is low.\n\nThe detailed child results are in n5.r1 (debt) and n6.r1 (equity).","ttft_ms":1243,"type":"result","duration_ms":61178,"uuid":"9927f45b-4770-4c1c-abd6-220fc42bdd0d","ttft_stream_ms":744,"time_to_request_ms":73,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":11,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":6,"input_attachments":14,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":4,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":6,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":3,"request_build":4},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":23,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":61,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":189,"proces